# Toolly repository text/binary normalization.
#
# The Gradle wrapper jar is committed as base64 text (see gradlew) because
# GitHub's browser contents API cannot preserve binary bytes. On checkouts
# with core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows Git default), Git would rewrite
# this file's line endings to CRLF and corrupt the base64 payload, breaking
# ./gradlew locally. Force it to be treated as text with LF-only normalization
# so the checked-out bytes always match what gradlew's SHA-256 check expects.
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar.base64 text eol=lf

# Real binary assets: never apply line-ending conversion.
*.jar -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
